==== Hardware Unbricking ====
A common issue with these devices is a hardware brick (LEDs remain off, device drawing current) caused by faulty ceramic capacitors on the 12v input line, near the regulators.

Check these three capacitors for low-impedance (i.e. short-circuit, capacitor becomes very hot when applying power and may even look damaged) and remove / replace:

{{http://sebastianschaper.net/openwrt/fritzbox_7360_typically_faulty_capacitors.jpg?500x0}}

===== Troubleshooting =====
**OpenWrt 21.02 switch issues**

Starting from the OpenWrt 21.02, there is a nasty bug which renders device switch unusable. Numerous reports show incorrect link speeds on LAN 1&2 and LAN 3&4 and absence of traffic activity. 
[[https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/8833|Bug details here]] 

**Poor NAT performance**

In case of 1 WAN / 3 LAN networking setup there seems to be a [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/how-can-we-make-the-lantiq-xrx200-devices-faster/9724/192|poor networking performance]] on WAN port with speeds around ~30-40 Mbit/sec.  This issue is resolved by turning on //Software flow offloading//.  Go to luci --> Network --> firewall and enable it in the settings.


